# Editor Palette Categories Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Replace the flat bottom palette bar in `MazeEditor3D` with three category tabs — Structure / Traversal / Traps — so the palette can hold many more piece types without shrinking thumbnails or hiding pieces behind scroll arrows.

**Architecture:** `PieceDB` gains a `PieceCategory` enum and a `Category` lookup — the single source of truth for which tab a piece lives in. `MazeEditor3D` builds every palette cell exactly once at startup (thumbnail `SubViewport`s are expensive and must not be rebuilt), then toggles cell `Visible` when the active tab changes. Nothing else in the editor changes.

**Tech Stack:** Godot 4.6.2 Mono (C#), Godot `Control` UI built imperatively in code — this project has no `.tscn`-authored UI for the editor.

