- Do not touch stair rotation logic, `AddStairRamp`, or `PlayerController.FloorMaxAngle` (see `CLAUDE.md` — solved architecture, do not revert).
- Existing saved mazes must keep loading. `PieceType` is serialized by **ordinal** (numeric position), not by name, through `System.Text.Json` — `MazeSerializer` registers no `JsonStringEnumConverter`. Appending or renaming enum members is safe; **reordering or removing an existing member silently corrupts every saved maze**, since every stored ordinal would then point at a different `PieceType`. [Corrected 2026-08-31 final-review pass — the rule itself ("append only") was always right and was followed; only the stated reason was wrong. See `JOURNAL.md`.]

